  "lineage": "Assyrian Church of the East liturgical chant, the canonical sacred-music tradition of the East-Syriac (Edessene) rite, descending from the Mesopotamian early-Christian community at Edessa and Nisibis. The Assyrian Beth Gazo collection comprises canonical melodies organized through an eight-mode system distinct from but related to the West-Syriac (Antiochene) Beth Gazo. Liturgical language is classical Syriac (Eastern dialect). The post-1915 Sayfo and Iraqi-Syrian displacement disrupted Hakkari-Mesopotamian transmission infrastructure; the Patriarchate (currently seated in Erbil) and diaspora communities in Chicago, Detroit, and Sydney sustain practice.",
